# Vauxhall Mokka compact SUV, 2012-2016.
#
# The first Mokka: the small crossover on the Gamma II platform with the
# high seating position and the chunky lower body. UK showrooms from
# November 2012; replaced by the Mokka X in October 2016.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Mokka
#
# Dimensions 4.280 x 1.775 x 1.646 m, wheelbase 2.555 m (Wikipedia infobox,
# cross-checked against Vauxhall launch material giving 4.28 m).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the flank is
# traced from it.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Mokka June 2012 brochure for model year 2012:
# Royal Blue solid, Summit White and Velvet Red brilliant, and Sovereign
# Silver, Carbon Flash, Satin Steel Grey and Boracay Blue metallic. Weights
# 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 70/285, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro November 2012; retires staggered 2016-2019 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-a.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-a.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-mokka-a/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the lamp internals, mirrors and alloy detail are
# simplified; the rear glass is smaller and the rear skid plate shallower than
# in the photographs.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallMokkaA(RoyalBlue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
